UID:m4nfel85f88cnqeuq7no6sv7to@google.com
CREATED:20141028T223922Z
DESCRIPTION:Early Christianity from a Jewish perspective\nFor five Thursday
 s in November through December 11 from 7:30 – 9 Beth Ami will sponsor this 
 class in room 12/13 (no class on Thanksgiving) Taught by Beth Ami member an
 d former Resident Head of the Christian Mission in Jerusalem\, Ishie Petloc
 k. The course will cover the time-span from the start of Christianity as a 
 Jewish sect to its adoption by the Roman Emperor in the 4th century as the 
 state religion.\n\nThere will be no required reading\, but most material wi
 ll be taken from the writings of Professor Amy Jill Levine of Vanderbilt Un
 iversity\, especially her edition of: The Jewish Annotated New Testament\, 
 Oxford University Press\, 2011. (with Marc Brettler) There will be no charg
 e for the course. For any questions e-mail Jeffrey Sheff (jssheff@gmail.com
 )
LAST-MODIFIED:20141028T225607Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Ami  (room 12/13)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Adult Education Class - "Early Christianity from a Jewish perspecti
 ve"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
