BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20171117T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20171117T180000
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:75hllms7io8vhk136f52ho957o@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20171117T193000
CREATED:20170801T192442Z
DESCRIPTION:"The Challenge of Coexisting" Friday night speakers \n\nFriday 
 November 17\, speakers from the Beit HaGefen Arab-Jewish Cultural Center on
  the art of shared living in Haifa.\n\nThe city of Haifa is unusual in the 
 Israeli human landscape\, offering an intercultural expanse that constitute
 s a model for building a shared society of Jews and Arabs\, veteran Israeli
 s and immigrants from the East and from the West. Founded in 1963\, Beit Ha
 Gefen is a cultural center which seeks to create shared egalitarian spaces 
 that contain the variety of identities and cultures in Haifa\, and in Israe
 l in general.\n\n\n5:30 to 6:00 - Asaf & Ulfat children's presentation (reg
 ular Shabat services will be provided).\n6:00 to 7:00 - Dinner. Adults $15\
 , Kids $3\, family $18 (RSVP required) \n7:00 to 8:30 - Asaf & Ulfat's pres
