UID:60pahvp4sv18tft56i0ct07vqr@google.com
CREATED:20190805T193401Z
DESCRIPTION:PANTHER IN THE BASEMENT with the BOOK GROUP \n\n Amos Oz's  PAN
 THER IN THE BASEMENT (Fiction\, 155 pgs.\, Hebrew.1994\; English trans. 199
 7) is the next read for the Adult Ed.-sponsored drop-in book  group. It tak
 es place in the summer of 1947 in Palestine under the British Mandate.  A 1
 2-year-old Jewish boy befriends a British soldier to improve his English\, 
 only to find himself branded as a traitor by his friends.  A coming of age 
 novel with a difference. . . \n\nWe will meet Wed.\, Aug. 28\, 7 PM.\, in o
 ur multi-purpose room.  Open to all CBA members and friends.  Come join us 
 for lively discussion.  Also\, a couple of mini book reports on other curre
 nt reading.  Refreshments.   A few copies\, including 1 in Hebrew\, borrowe
 d from the SF Jewish Community Lib. will be available July 31 in the CBA Of
 fice.  If none in box when you look for it\, give me a call or if other com
 ments.  Linda 544-4532.  I'll find someone who has finished reading the boo
 k.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190805T193401Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Book Discussion Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
