DESCRIPTION:https://jewishfed.org/news/events/emergency-preparedness-fairAl
 l are welcome. Bring your neighbor! The Jewish community is partnering with
  local organizations and first responders to help you plan ahead and know w
 hat actions to take in the event of a future crisis.BE INFORMED. KNOW HOW T
 O RESPOND.Presentations on home safety\, medical response\, survival strate
 gies and the 911 system from local PD and fire department. Practice skills 
 such as CPR and first aid. Learn important numbers to have on hand.HAVE A P
 LAN. GET TO KNOW YOUR NEIGHBORInformational materials to develop your perso
 nal plan. Get your neighborhood ready. Checklists and ideas for “go” bags a
 nd to shelter in place.BUILD YOUR CONFIDENCESit with companion canines\, cr
 awl in fire engines and patrol cars\, visit an animal mobile command center
 .Enjoy food trucks\, water stations\, bounce house\, and secure children’s 
 playground.For more information\, contact info@sfjcf.orgWith gratitude to o
 ur participating local organizations: Sonoma County Animal Services Ready M
 arin * American Heart Association * Sonoma County Auxiliary Comm Services *
  Santa Rosa Fire Dept * American Red Cross * Sonoma County Sheriff * Santa 
 Rosa Police Department * COPE/Files For Life * Sonoma County Council on Agi
 ng * PG
LAST-MODIFIED:20190531T202717Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Ami \, 4676 Mayette Avenue • Free parking\, Sant
 a Rosa
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Emergency Preparedness Fair  
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
