BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART:20081114T033000Z
DTEND:20081114T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:CSVConverte1c63fb77baf2860d18da58e501d2231
CREATED:19000101T120000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course explores Israel's two histories\, Biblical and mode
 rn. In the first session\, students will travel on a visually rich virtual 
 guided tour of Bilblical Israel (1200-400 BCE). In the second session\, we'
 ll introduce the brief\, but dramatic history of moderd Israel to date\, to
 uching on the central achievments and conflicts of the Jewish State. In the
  process\, we will also explore the connections between the two Israels\, p
 ast and present. <br>\nThe first session will be held at Shomrei Torah on W
 ed. Nov. 12 and the second session will be at Beth Ami on Thurs. Nov. 13.<b
 r>\nTuition: $18/public $10/members of all congregations/JCC\nFor more info
 rmation and/or to register: log on to www.lehrhaus.org or call (510)845-642
 0 x10
LAST-MODIFIED:20210101T000000Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Understanding Israel: Connecting the Biblical and Modern Land
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
