UID:35gic1eudjhi6hsndtfn98m988@google.com
CREATED:20220118T202802Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u>&nbsp\;The event will be held via Zoom <br>Th
 e theme of this year’s commemoration will be Speaking Up and Standing Up. T
 hree local Holocaust survivors or descendants will be sharing how they were
  helped by “upstanders” who did the right thing.<br><br>There will be music
 al performances as well as candle lighting by Jewish&nbsp\;survivors\; ligh
 ters for the Roma\, Gays &amp\; Lesbians\, Disabled\, Righteous&nbsp\;Genti
 les\, and Political Prisoners\; and those targeted by genocide. In&nbsp\;ad
 dition\, you will be able to include the names of loved ones who were<br>vi
 ctims of the Shoah in this year’s Memorial Book.&nbsp\;<u></u></html-blob><
 br><html-blob><br></html-blob><br><html-blob>The program is free\, but regi
 stration is required to access the Zoom link.&nbsp\;</html-blob><br><html-b
 lob>Information about how to register for the event and submit names for th
 e&nbsp\;</html-blob>&nbsp\;memorial book will be posted in February at:<br>
 <html-blob>&nbsp\;https://www.jccsoco.org/main/yom-hashoah-commemoration/.&
 nbsp\;</html-blob><br><html-blob>&nbsp\;You can view last&nbsp\;</html-blob
 >&nbsp\;year’s commemoration using the same link.
LAST-MODIFIED:20220118T203147Z
LOCATION:Zoom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sonoma County Yom HaShoah Commemoration 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
