CREATED:20210115T201057Z
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, January 18\, 2021 *5 Shevat 57815:00 PM - 6:00 PM on a
  separate Zoom.  Join synagogue partners from across the nation:\nKol Emeth
 \, Palo Alto\, CA\nBeth Hillel B'nai Emunah\, Chicago\, IL\nBeth Ami\, Sant
 a Rosa\, CA\nBeth Am\, Los Angeles\, CA\nTemple of Aaron\, St. Paul\, MN\nK
 ol Rinah\, St. Louis\, MO\nBeth Tzedek\, Buffalo\, NY\nfor a joyous celebra
 tion of Dr. Martin Luther King\, Jr.'s life. We'll reflect on the ideas and
  religious texts that inspired his leadership\, and learn with some of toda
 y's spiritual and political leaders\, who continue to be motivated by his w
 ords and work. for a joyous celebration of Dr. Martin Luther King\, Jr.'s l
 ife. We'll reflect on the ideas and religious texts that inspired his leade
 rship\, and learn with some of today's spiritual and political leaders\, wh
 o continue to be motivated by his words and work.\nOur speakers will includ
 e:\nRabbi Debra A. Bowen of Congregation Temple Beth'El (Philadelphia\, PA)
  \nDr. John H. Eaves\, educator\, activist\, and former Congressional candi
 date (Atlanta\, GA) \nRev. Kaloma A. Smith\, Pastor of University AME Zion 
 Church (Palo Alto\, CA)\n\nWe hope that you'll participate in a morning ser
 vice event for Mitzvah Day\, and join us in the evening for music\, reading
  and sharing as we commemorate Dr. King.\n\nRegister for Zoom url here:  ht
 tps://kolemeth.shulcloud.com/event/the-message-of-mlk-day-now.html
LAST-MODIFIED:20210115T201057Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:MLK Day program
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
