UID:7iul2q72q9bqq6f5j3dt9s7ifg@google.com
CREATED:20221121T191502Z
DESCRIPTION:\nWe know that Jewish holiday food is full not only of calories
 \, but symbolism. We eat latkes fried in oil to remind us of the oil that l
 asted eight days. But why do we put applesauce on our latkes? On Sunday Dec
 ember 18 it will symbolize that the apple doesn't fall far from the tree: w
 e will sing with and listen to the Chanukah music of the wonderful and fabu
 lous Susy Boimoil Starr and her wonderful and fabulous son Jeremy Lipsin.\n
 \nThe latkes will be\, as usual\, pretty wonderful as well. Volunteer to he
 lp! Leave a message in the office for Myra Stern-Thomas\, Kitchen Committee
  chair.\n\n4:30 - 5:20 schmooze\, play a card/ board game\n5:20 songs\, a s
 hort service\, light candles (Bring your Chanukiah and 2 candles!)\n6:00 - 
 7:30 Latke (and salad) dinner served\n7:30 Birkat HaMazon\nRSVP to the Beth
  Ami office by Wednesday Dec. 14\, or we won’t have enough latkes! Cost: FR
 EE but donations accepted with gratitude.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221206T184530Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Chanukah Party
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
