UID:nepkl98kos1l40ntee04eqrvmo@google.com
CREATED:20111011T210043Z
DESCRIPTION:Section 1 - For Nursery and Religious School Parents. Parents a
 re the primary educators of their children and should be active participant
 s in the effort to help their children understand the "whys" of living a Je
 wish life in the 21st century. Yet\, many Jewish parents have not had the o
 pporunity to study Judaism as adults and gain a mature understanding of wha
 t is one of the most sphisticated relisious systems in the world. We will e
 xplore the values and spritual meaning behind various defining elements of 
 Jewish religious experience\, including prayer\, Shabbat\, holidays\, kashr
 ut\, ethics\, and Torah study. We will also learn contemporary expresions o
 f faith in God and analyze attempts to answer the question\; who wrote the 
 Bible? We will also discuss the best ways to enable young minds to grasp th
 ese concepts.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230220T062032Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Ami
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Adult Ed. #101 - Why Be Jewish? Section 1
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
