BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART:20130515T020000Z
DTEND:20130515T090000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:h85f5oc5rfkubo8085uno9mh98@google.com
CREATED:20130418T191923Z
DESCRIPTION:Informal study will continue until dawn! This is our night of r
 evelation - when the Children of Israel received Torah. And we are receivin
 g it still today. Join rabbis and teachers from around Sonoma County as we 
 look at the ways in which Torah is still coming at us\; how our inherited a
 nd innovated wisdom informs who we are in the world. \nDelicious dairy trea
 ts will be served. Childcare available until 9 PM. Formal study sessions ru
 n until 2 AM\, after which informal study will continue for as long as teac
 hers and students can hold out\, ending with shacharit at dawn! Teachers in
 clude:\nCarolyn Shoshana Fershtman\, PhD\nRabbi Jerry Danzig\nRabbi George 
 Gittleman\nReb Judith Goleman\nReb Irwin Keller\nRabbi Stephanie Kramer\nRa
 bbi Mordecai Miller\nSarah Miller\nDavid and Andrea Rubinstein\nRabbi Mende
 l Wolvovsky\nThis event is strictly scent-free and smoke-free. Please\, ple
 ase\, be mindful so this holy night of study can be safe for everyone
LAST-MODIFIED:20230220T063049Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Ami - Social Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tikkun Leyl Shavout Study Session
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART:20130228T030000Z
DTEND:20130228T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:01agvgiptkal413ubdps7937to@google.com
CREATED:20130211T193505Z
DESCRIPTION:Len Lyons will give a lecture on Black Jews in America on Wedne
 sday evening\, February 27\, at 7:00 pm on the occasion of Black History Mo
 nth. Professor Lyons is a prolific teacher and lecturer in many diverse fie
 lds\, and has done extensive research on Black Jews in America\, in particu
 lar Chicago and NYC. This event will take place in the Beth Ami Social Hall
 . 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230220T062807Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Ami
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Adult Ed. Event: Black Jews in America
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
