DESCRIPTION:November 3 is our first Book Discussion meeting. New\nmembers\,
  male or female\, are most welcome.\nOnce again we invite you to participat
 e in a book discussion\nseries that has attracted many folks who love books
 \nthat stretch your mind and challenge your imagination and\nto discuss the
 m with like-minded people.\nWe meet at Congregation Beth Ami on the first\n
 Wednesday of each month at 10 a.m. beginning in November.\nHere is our sc h
 edule:\n1) *The Believers\, by Zoe Heller Nov. 3\nDiscussion Leader: Ethel 
 Schy\n2) Nothing Sacred: the Truth About Judaism Dec. 1\nby Douglas Rushkof
 f\n3 Ten Green Bottles\, by Vivian J. Kaplan Jan. 5\n4) *Natasha and Other 
 Stories\, by David Bezmozgis Feb. 2\n5) Letters from the Earth\, by Mark Tw
 ain Mar. 2\n6) When a Crocodile Eats the Sun\, by Peter Godwin Apr. 6\n7) P
 rophet’s Wife\, by Milton Steinberg May 4\n8) The Help\, by Kathryn Stocket
 t June 1\n9) Crossing Mandelbaum Gate\, by Kai Bird July 6
LAST-MODIFIED:20230220T062503Z
LOCATION:Room 12/13
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Library Book Club Mtg.
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
