BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20241110T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20241110T123000
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:471tbhjd4b7jii52fie05o8ut5@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20241110T103000
CREATED:20241011T194028Z
DESCRIPTION:This is a walk that’s not about the walk. We’ll speak about God
  and the wonders of creation. We’ll stop along the way to admire the beauty
  of nature and share thoughts and feelings.  How often have you walked alon
 g without noticing your surroundings\, without looking with amazement at th
 e dragonfly\, the egret\, the lupine\; without hearing the woodpecker and t
 he geese? That won’t happen at Torah on the Trail. Join us and see for your
 self.\n \nOur first walk\, on Sunday\, November 10th at 10:30\, will be aro
 und Spring Lake. Fast and slow walkers welcome. Allow about two hours for w
 alking\, stopping\, and sharing. If you won’t be going to the breakfast bef
 orehand\, email the rabbi for the meeting place: rabbi@bethamisr.org
LAST-MODIFIED:20250219T221630Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Torah on Trails 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
