RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20120301T193000
CREATED:20111216T203936Z
DESCRIPTION:Course No. 202: Contemporary Issues: A Jewish Ethical Perspecti
 ve.  \nWe will study what Jewish religious authorities\, from Biblical time
 s to our own day\, have had to say about a variety of topics\, including: B
 usiness Practices\; Ecology\; Medical Dilemmas\; Religious Plural-ism.  We 
 will explore the values that have shaped Jewish approaches to these matters
  and consider what guidance our tradition can give us as we address these c
 ritical issues.  \nTaught by Rabbi Rembaum on Thursdays at 7:30 pm (when he
  is present)\, resuming January 5. Rooms 12/13.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20240918T041549Z
LOCATION:Room 12/13
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Adult Ed. Class #202
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
