RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20241113T120000
CREATED:20241011T193725Z
DESCRIPTION:Starting with the book Why Be Different? A Look into Judaism\, 
 we’ll use stories and questions to deepen our understanding of Judaism. Fro
 m tackling troubling questions to applying Jewish teachings to everyday lif
 e\, we’ll learn together each month.\n \nOh\, and don’t forget the food. Or
 der a veggie wrap or tuna sandwich (box lunch\, chips and a drink for $12).
  Please order through the office at 707-360-3000 by the Monday prior to cla
 ss.
LAST-MODIFIED:20250203T191740Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn with Rabbi Koas
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20120108T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20120108T110000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;COUNT=6;INTERVAL=2;BYDAY=SU
EXDATE;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20120219T100000
EXDATE;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20120205T100000
EXDATE;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20120318T100000
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:1fggi87kljjt6mo6dknreqjajs@google.com
CREATED:20111216T203532Z
DESCRIPTION:Course No. 103: Why Be Jewish? \nFor Nursery and Religious Scho
 ol parents\, grandparents and all others.  \nParents are the primary educat
 ors of their children and should be active participants in the effort to he
 lp their children understand the “whys” of living a Jewish life in the 21st
  century.  We will explore the values and spiritual meaning behind various 
 defining elements of Jewish religious experience\, including prayer\, Shabb
 at\, holidays\, Kashrut\, ethics and Torah study.  We will help parents and
  grandparents understand our tradition and transmit it to the upcoming gene
 ration. \nTaught by Rabbi Rembaum on the 1st  and 3rd Sunday of each month 
 at 10:00 am\, resuming January 8 in the Sanctuary.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20240918T041537Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Adult Ed. Course #103
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART:20130407T210000Z
DTEND:20130407T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:gm2kg9d6p9gfs3qtamqbvf7uhg@google.com
CREATED:20130313T215632Z
DESCRIPTION:The Future of Holocaust Memory\nHow will we preserve and insure
  the memory of the Shoah when there are no \nliving survivors? What role an
 d responsibility do future generations have? Can \nhistorical and cultural 
 reminders transmit the memory and messages of this \ncatastrophic event?\nG
 uest speaker: Jack Weinstein\, San Francisco Bay Area Director\nFacing Hist
 ory and Ourselves\nFree. Everyone is welcome. \nSpecial yellow Holocaust me
 morial candles will be \navailable for attendees for lighting at home.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230220T063522Z
LOCATION:The Friedman Event Center
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Yom HaShoah Commemoration
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
