DESCRIPTION:<table><tbody><tr><td><br><br><table><tbody><tr><td><br><p><str
 ong>Immigration Issues in Our Community<br>Congregation Beth Ami Friday\, A
 ugust 1</strong><br><br>6:00 pm Kabbalat Shabbat service with Rabbi Koas<br
 >6:45 pm special Shabbat chicken dinner<br>7:30 pm speakers Max Alper\, Exe
 cutive Director of<br>North Bay Jobs with Justice\, and Santa Rosa Mayor Ma
 rk Stapp </p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><table><tb
 ody><tr><td><br><br><table><tbody><tr><td></td></tr></tbody></table></td></
 tr></tbody></table><table><tbody><tr><td><br><br><table><tbody><tr><td><br>
 <p>Come learn about the lives of immigrant workers in our community and the
 ir current efforts to have successful jobs so they can build a more just fu
 ture. Hear about the efforts by the city of Santa Rosa to protect our immig
 rant community. Learn about the parallels of their struggles and the hardsh
 ips shared by our Jewish immigrant parents\, grandparents and ancestors.<br
 ><br>Please make your reservation if you are eating dinner by the preceding
  Wednesday at noon. Special <strong>chicken dinner </strong>is $20 for memb
 ers age 12 and up. $25 for age 12 and up non-members. $9 for Under 12. Some
  scholarships available. Call 707-360-3000 or email <a href="mailto:office@
 bethamisr.org" target="_blank">office@bethamisr.org</a>.</p></td></tr></tbo
 dy></table></td></tr></tbody></table>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250723T202037Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Dinner
TRANSP:OPAQUE
