BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Ami
DTSTART:20260208T183000Z
DTEND:20260208T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T040530Z
UID:76pkotn3a0k9rj4esk81mk8gsg@google.com
CREATED:20251222T234943Z
DESCRIPTION:Tu B’Shevat\, the birthday of the trees\, is really about fruit
  trees.\nBut when we live so close to some of the oldest and tallest\ntrees
  in California\, we periodically have to take this\nopportunity to go and a
 dmire them.\n\nWe’ll meet in the parking lot at Beth Ami at 10:00 am to\nca
 rpool and meet those arriving on their own at the parking\nlot at the Picni
 c Area at 10:45 am.\n\nBring food to eat\, and share: including something i
 nvolving\nnuts and fruits that come from trees. We will walk on a\nwheelcha
 ir and stroller accessible nature trail before lunch\,\nand after lunch tho
 se who wish may take a 2.2 mile East Ridge\nTrail loop\, or a longer valley
  floor walk.\n\nThe parking lots at the Visitors Center near the entrance o
 r at\nthe Picnic Area are both $10. 00 per vehicle\, $9 if there is\nanyone
  over 62 in the car. If it is raining at 10:00 AM we can\nmeet and stay in 
 the multi purpose room.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260105T195915Z
LOCATION:Armstrong Redwoods State Natural Reserve\, 17000 Armstrong Woods R
 d\, Guerneville\, CA 95446\, USA
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tu B'Shevat at Armstrong Redwoods 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
