UID:1tpj423hvqtob548vusflug19d@google.com
CREATED:20260203T215925Z
DESCRIPTION:<h4>Thursday\, April 2 at 6:30 p.m. Led by Rabbi Ron Koas</h4><
 p>Welcoming all ages\, affiliations\, interfaith &amp\; LGBT communities\, 
 members\, and non-members.<br>The meal will be fish\, dairy and vegetarian\
 , with a special dessert.<br>Members: adults $40\, youths $16<br>Family Max
 imum: $100\, under 6 years old free.<br>Non-members: Adults $45<br>Youth $1
 8\, Family Maximum: $120\, under 6 years old free.<br>Subsidies available s
 o all can attend. <b>Reservations Deadline Tuesday March 31 by noon.</b></p
 ><p><b><br></b>See the Shofar newsletter for festival services throughout t
 he holiday\, in person and on Zoom. All are welcome.</p><p>The Pesach Guide
  from the Rabbinical Assembly is here: <a href="https://www.rabbinicalassem
 bly.org/jewish-law/kashrut/pesah-guide">https://www.rabbinicalassembly.org/
 jewish-law/kashrut/pesah-guide</a></p><p>If you wish to sell your Hametz fo
 r the duration of Pesach\, please do one of the following:<br>1) Print out 
 the form <a href="https://bethamisr.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Sale-of-
 Hametz-for-Pesach-5786.pdf">Sale of Hametz for Pesach 5786</a> and email it
  to office@bethamisr.org a copy of it (with the names and addresses) to the
  synagogue.<br>2) Print and fill out the form and bring it to the synagogue
  office.<br>We must have your form by 10:00 am on Tuesday\, March 31\, 2026
  in order to be included in the sale for this year.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260326T231025Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Community Seder
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
